<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea to absorb 700 bln won through repos.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea to absorb 700 bln won through repos.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea said on Monday it has decided to absorb 700 billion won from commercial banks through five-day repurchase agreements (repos).  </p>
<p>&quot;The central bank has decided to soak up 700 billion won for five days due to abundant liquidity in the market,&quot; a central bank official told Reuters by telephone.</p>
<p>&quot;This is unlikely to poise any (liquidity) problems on banking institutions.&quot;</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
